    {
      "id": "FACT-0057",
      "kind": "observed_fact",
      "status": "active",
      "statement": "R03 Step4 owner review identifies that Habitat angled looks like a wider rectangle rather than a clearly sloping board. Static inspection confirms a real camera tilt at offset (0,80,60), about 53.13 degrees above the XZ board, but orthographic projection with no yaw leaves a flat axis-aligned rectangle. Vertical foreshortening is 0.8; when height limits Fit, compensating magnification makes width 1.25 times top-down width. Flat unshaded materials provide little additional depth information.",
      "uncertainty": "Diagnosis combines inspected implementation with the two owner-supplied screenshots; no new build or runtime measurement. Camera geometry is tilted, so calling it only an artificial board stretch would be inaccurate. Visual intent remains unsatisfied in this owner review; other Step4 work is not rejected wholesale, and overall acceptance is not inferred.",
      "source_refs": [
        "SRC-0270",
        "SRC-0271",
        "SRC-0276"
      ],
      "origin": {
        "type": "owner_review_and_static_code_inspection",
        "actor": "Genepool Analyzer",
        "recorded_at_utc": "2026-09-08T09:05:37.278164+00:00",
        "owner_feedback": "This is great but I am confused on your implementation of angled view; screenshots show a fatter board, and the owner asks whether the view should actually look angled.",
        "attachments": [
          "codex-clipboard-ab5d4bda-0fb0-4b30-a95b-d0598e2e7286.png",
          "codex-clipboard-b4f25910-572f-4cd7-ab27-9a7cbc4dfb2e.png"
        ]
      },
      "derivation": {
        "locators": [
          "BoardView3D.cs:86-89 (foreshortening/Fit),118-121 (orthographic),290-314 (mapping/camera)",
          "BoardView3D.Materials.cs:7-8,54-55 (unshaded flat patches)",
          "VerificationRunner.Step4.cs:26-66 (Boolean/round-trip checks),217 onward (top-down rendered pixel/input checks),271 (preview capture)"
        ],
        "external_reference": {
          "url": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_camera3d.html",
          "locator": "ProjectionType: PROJECTION_PERSPECTIVE and PROJECTION_ORTHOGONAL",
          "retrieved_at_utc": "2026-09-08T09:05:37.278164+00:00",
          "claim": "Orthographic projection does not reduce apparent object size with distance; perspective does."
        },
        "verification_gap": "Existing angled Boolean and CellAt(CellCenter) round trips share the affine mapping; they do not prove perceived depth. Inspected material/pick pixel test switches to top-down. Generated angled screenshots were visually reviewed but the widened-rectangle problem was missed. Previous measured passes remain valid within their exercised scope.",
        "recommendation": "Keep top-down for exact reading; revise angled toward a visibly oblique camera with gentle perspective and slight yaw. Validate same-frame projected corners and near/far cell sizes, then rendered appearance, picking, panning, minimap, culling and action alignment. This is an Analyzer recommendation, not a newly accepted design or implementation."
      },
